FAIL: Uint8Array view with byteOffset 3: only its 3 bytes are sent
FAIL: Uint8Array view: Content-Length is the view's byteLength
FAIL: DataView(buf, 2, 3): honours byteOffset and byteLength
FAIL: Int16Array(buf, 2, 2): 2 elements = 4 bytes from offset 2
FAIL: Float32Array: the element type is ignored, its bytes are sent
FAIL: whole-buffer Uint8Array: its bytes, no Content-Type
FAIL: Blob: its bytes, mixed string and binary parts
FAIL: Blob: Content-Type is blob.type (already normalized)
FAIL: typeless Blob: its bytes and NO Content-Type
FAIL: File: bytes and its type
FAIL: sliced Blob: the slice's bytes and type
FAIL: fetch FormData: Content-Type multipart/form-data; boundary=<token>
FAIL: fetch FormData: exact multipart bytes (normalized, escaped, File parts typed)
FAIL: empty FormData: just the closing delimiter
FAIL: Blob body + page Content-Type: the page's value wins
FAIL: Request(view): bytes copied when the Request was built
FAIL: fetch(request.clone()): the clone carries the body
FAIL: Request FormData: Content-Type multipart/form-data; boundary=<token>
FAIL: Request FormData: exact multipart bytes (normalized, escaped, File parts typed)
FAIL: new Response(view): the view's own bytes, copied at construction
FAIL: XHR Uint8Array view with byteOffset: only its bytes, no Content-Type
FAIL: XHR DataView with byteOffset: only its bytes
FAIL: XHR Blob: bytes and blob.type
FAIL: XHR FormData: Content-Type multipart/form-data; boundary=<token>
FAIL: XHR FormData: exact multipart bytes (normalized, escaped, File parts typed)
